      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2: Added fairness constraint on exeReady to fix 3 failing liveness properties (entry0_progress, entry1_progress, entry2_progress). Error type: setup_error. Root cause: io.exeReady was completely unconstrained, allowing it to stay 00 forever, making issue signals impossible to fire. Since flush(0) was also never asserted and opsReady(0) never deasserted, none of the liveness escape conditions could be met. Fix: Added a 3-bit exeReadyTimer that counts consecutive cycles where io.exeReady.orR is false, and assumes exeReadyTimer < 7 (i.e., at least one execution unit must be ready at least once every 7 cycles). This fairness assumption prevents the vacuously unsatisfiable environment while allowing realistic idle periods. All 17 original assertion labels are preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions needed as this is a setup-level constraint addition, not an assertion repair.",
